  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nContinued the trend of decreasing dewpoints during the afternoon\nhours the next few days. Also decreased the temperatures again across\ncentral ohio east of Columbus and added patchy frost in. Will\ncontinue to highlight frost in the HWO as well across this area. With\nwinds off of the lake also will have the potential for some fog\nacross the north in addition to river valley fog. Have mention in \nthe HWO for fog across the north. \n\nOtherwise, dry conditions are expected through at least the middle of\nnext week. High temperatures will be in the 60s and 70s and lows in\nthe upper 30s to low 50s.",
